{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0DDB", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-torsion}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bc256a2b655261f099302f387e4c300c70673c266065f2cb95243d0a6c725337", "source_text": "Torsion sheaves", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c690843fe60309e0fb3e63f4fb3c623062b13bcf54be22464550719a60183ba7", "unit_id": "tag:0DDB:title"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DDB", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$D(\\mathcal{C})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-lemma-torsion}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:626d2e831119ab8011cee450fc1d03468a6c19979a21ee4c2206f8cd0c79eb98", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5fceea17858faa336e75f17755c10c5eaf4e64748590682eefe2c28aa23bf682", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA brief section on torsion abelian sheaves and their <ACCENT_0001>tale cohomology.\nLet <MATH_0001> be a site. We have shown in\nCohomology on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthat any object in <MATH_0002> whose cohomology sheaves are\ntorsion sheaves, can be represented by a complex all of whose terms\nare torsion.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b7da27d1d48fe04ae9948e09a51579d53ac5b56d4d556071a720a80dba7aed50", "unit_id": "tag:0DDB:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DDB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$H^n_\\etale(X, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0005": "$n$", "MATH_0006": "$K$", "MATH_0007": "$D^+(X_\\etale)$", "MATH_0008": "$H^n_\\etale(X, K)$", "MATH_0009": "$n$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-torsion-cohomology}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4d2bdc374adada05c6fb83190ea17e8d070f0c6e323e39b936fa5a25e3bba2f9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:76faf563633360522d78c390a3693959b5aac2d7e52fc9f7ae20a2e5dcc64df7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is a torsion abelian sheaf on <MATH_0003>, then\n<MATH_0004> is a torsion abelian group for all <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0006> in <MATH_0007> has torsion cohomology sheaves, then\n<MATH_0008> is a torsion abelian group for all <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4127fb44801fa4cd47a72c0845be04247fa8323665123a084779e38ade863369", "unit_id": "tag:0DDC:statement"}
